# Fixed 2026-10-11, defect 608, lane b20-check: the shape beside it with the
# symbol a cell took until panel 209, `_: i64 @ f(1)`. Before the repair it
# was told `old_cell_symbol`, whose certain fix writes `@=` and so wrote the
# accepted wildcard cell; with the wildcard refused, that fix would have
# written a line refused again, two passes of `check --apply` for one line.
# Now `parse/annotation` leaves the wildcard's old `@` to the resolver, which
# tells it once, and the certain fix writes `=` where the `@` is.
#
# Corrected 2026-10-11, the same day, by batch 20's gate B: a line the
# parser reads with nothing said is one `fmt` prints, and it printed this
# `@` as `@=`, so `heroes probe --family multi` saw every comment beside it
# move (9 of 9 variants). The parser tells it again, `old_cell_symbol` in
# `cell_errors.old_symbol`'s words for the wildcard, its certain fix writing
# `=`: still one message and one pass, and `fmt` refuses the line as it
# refuses every line the parser recovers.

function f(x: i64) -> i64
    return x + 1

function main()
    _: i64 = f(1)  #~ old_cell_symbol
    print("done")
